{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track a control activation each time a touch activates a UIKit control, without a call on each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"control."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"The event","anchor":"The-event","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking\/ControlActivated"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this module when an app’s UIKit controls should track their own activations, such as a button","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tapped or a switch flipped. The discovery runs on iOS, iPadOS, tvOS, visionOS and Mac","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Catalyst, through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIWindowScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking\/ControlActivated","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", the event it tracks, builds on every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"platform, so a tracking plan or a server can name it. SwiftUI’s controls are never tracked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"automatically: give them ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackOnTap(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"macOS has no equivalent; give an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSControl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"track(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing is tracked until a window scene turns it on with ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"control is named after its ","type":"text"},{"code":"accessibilityIdentifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never its title or other text, which may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a person’s data, and carries its kind, the first public UIKit class it is (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"UIButton\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). By","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default a control without an identifier is skipped:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import UIKit","","final class CartViewController: UIViewController {","    let checkOut = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","","    override func viewDidLoad() {","        super.viewDidLoad()","        checkOut.accessibilityIdentifier = \"checkout-button\"  \/\/ tracked as ControlActivated(control: \"checkout-button\", kind: \"UIButton\")","        view.addSubview(checkOut)","    }","}","","\/\/ In the scene delegate's scene(_:willConnectTo:options:), beside the scene's tracker:","windowScene.traitOverrides.tracker = tracker","windowScene.trackControlsAutomatically()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Give "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackControlsAutomatically"},{"type":"text","text":" a closure to rename a control or skip it: it gets each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiscoveredControl"},{"type":"text","text":", with its identifier, kind and screen, and returns the event, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":". Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s context carries the control’s screen, the type of the view controller it is in, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenKey"},{"type":"text","text":", unless the tracker’s enrichers set one."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A touch that ends off the control tracks nothing, and neither do activations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without a touch, such as VoiceOver’s, or actions the app sends itself with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sendActions(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"except to a control the last touch was on and didn’t activate. Each activation goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the tracker the control’s traits hold, so each scene keeps its own. The scene adds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture recognizer to each of its windows that never recognizes, so it holds up no touch, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"swizzles nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This documentation is built on macOS, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"UIWindowScene","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"stopTrackingControlsAutomatically()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscoveredControl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", have no pages here; their doc","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comments are in the sources.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also covers screen views and the app’s lifecycle."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"AutomaticControlTracking","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"AutomaticControlTracking"}],"externalID":"AutomaticControlTracking"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking/ControlActivated":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking\/ControlActivated","abstract":[{"text":"Someone activated the control named ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking\/ControlActivated\/control","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", such as by tapping a button or flipping a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"switch: what ","type":"text"},{"code":"trackControlsAutomatically(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks for each activation it discovers.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ControlActivated"}],"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking\/controlactivated","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ControlActivated"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"ControlActivated","type":"topic"},"doc://AutomaticControlTracking/documentation/AutomaticControlTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/automaticcontroltracking","title":"AutomaticControlTracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/AutomaticControlTracking\/documentation\/AutomaticControlTracking","abstract":[{"text":"Track a control activation each time a touch activates a UIKit control, without a call on each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"control.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.